  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Jakar510/Jakar.Json",
  "published": "2026-10-17T00:40:10.237Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.2.0 (breaking): buffer writers are generic and passed by ref, so struct and ref struct writers work without boxing: JsonCodec.WriteJson<T, TWriter>(in T, ref TWriter) (UTF-8), JsonCodec.WriteJsonUtf16<T, TWriter>(in T, ref TWriter), JsonCodec.WriteJsonArray<T, TWriter>(..., ref TWriter), JsonTypeCodec.Write<TWriter>(object?, ref TWriter), and the generated WriteJson<TWriter>(ref TWriter); the IBufferWriter<byte|char> overloads are gone. 10.1.0: initial release. Absorbs Jakar.SystemTextJson (IJsonModel<TSelf>, [JsonModel], JsonModel, RentedArray<T>, SerializeAsStringJsonConverter<T>; still in the Jakar.Extensions namespace, diagnostics JAKAR_JSON001-007 unchanged). One attribute, [JsonModel]: without a System.Text.Json context it's Jakar.Json only; with one it implements IJsonModel<TSelf> on Jakar.Json when that supports the type (faster, fewer allocations; the context's options mirrored), otherwise on System.Text.Json (JJSON016). [GenerateJson] and JJSON010 are gone.",
